From 7a6e7b028fa00950d36530ebf85208a4290a20ce Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chetan Mistry <chetan.mistry@morsemicro.com>
Date: Mon, 5 May 2025 08:15:26 +1000
Subject: [PATCH] Configure NetworkManager to talk to 2 WPA Supplicants

This change allows NetworkManager to comminucate with 2
WPA Supplicant services (wpa_supplicant and wpa_supplicant_s1g).
The intended usage is that wpa_supplicant_s1g handles all wifi connections
on MorseMicro/S1G radios and wpa_supplicant handles everything else.
It works by extending the supplicant manager and interface manager structures
to contain the extra information needed to communicate with the additional
supplicant.
It also dynamically identifies which interfaces are running on morse radios.

Signed-off-by: Chetan Mistry <chetan.mistry@morsemicro.com>
